				this one.</p> <div class="shadow-window-body bg-black font-chevyray flex flex-col justify-center items-center min-h-0 w-full "><div class="flex flex-row justify-between w-full items-center py-[6px] px-2 shadow-window-head bg-medium-gray"><!--[-1--><p>Claude/Codex</p><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--></div> <div class="p-[2px] flex min-h-0 grow flex-col justify-center items-center w-full"><div class="w-full p-3 text-left"><div class="flex flex-col gap-6 bg-pure-black p-4 leading-[1.8] shadow-input sm:p-5"><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-2"><p class="text-sm text-light-gray">You</p> <p>Use Sprite Fusion's explosion effect for my grenades: blow up where they land, with dirt in my ground's colour.</p></div> <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3"><p class="text-sm text-light-gray">Claude</p> <p>I found the explosion effect in Sprite Fusion's VFX library and built it into your game.</p> <img src="/images/pixel-art-vfx/explosion-dirt.webp" alt="Explosion pixel art effect playing in a game" width="320" height="200" loading="lazy" style="image-rendering: pixelated;" class="aspect-[16/10] w-full max-w-[320px] shadow-input"/></div></div></div><!----></div></div><!----> <div class="flex w-full sm:max-w-xs"><!--[-1--><button class="font-chevyrayOeuf  relative overflow-hidden px-2 py-[6px] bg-medium-gray hover:bg-light-gray flex flex-row justify-center items-center focus:outline-none svelte-103j0yv shadow-button w-full opacity-100"><span class="pointer-events-none absolute bottom-[3px] left-[3px] top-[3px] z-0 bg-medium-gray" style="width: 0%; transition-duration: 160ms; transition-property: width; transition-timing-function: linear;"></span> <span class="relative z-10 flex flex-row items-center justify-center space-x-[6px]"><p>Connect your AI agent</p><!----></span></button><!--]--><!---->  <dialog aria-label="Connect your AI agent" class="m-auto max-h-[calc(100dvh-24px)] w-[calc(100%-24px)] max-w-xl overflow-y-auto border-0 bg-transparent p-0 text-white backdrop:bg-pure-bl